Academic Block (Classrooms & Laboratories)
•	The Academic Block will house smart classrooms, lecture halls, and laboratories, ensuring a high-quality learning environment.
Smart Classrooms & Lecture Halls
•	Four fully equipped lecture halls with a seating capacity of 100–125 students each.
•	Smart boards, projectors, and digital content for interactive learning.
•	Wi-Fi-enabled classrooms to support online education and remote learning modules.
a. Classrooms
•	The institute will have dedicated smart classrooms with modern teaching aids such as audio-visual projectors, digital whiteboards, and e-learning modules.
•	Each classroom will have a seating capacity of 100–125 students, ensuring a comfortable and engaging learning environment.
•	The curriculum will be taught using an interactive pedagogy, including case studies, field visits, and simulation-based learning.

b. Laboratories
•	The institute will feature state-of-the-art, well-equipped laboratories for hands-on training in various aspects of veterinary sciences, including:
•	Veterinary Pharmacy Laboratory – Equipped with pharmaceutical instruments for drug formulation, compounding, and analysis of veterinary medicines.
•	Microbiology & Pathology Laboratory – To train students in diagnostics, disease identification, and microbiological analysis.
•	Pharmacology & Toxicology Laboratory – For studying the effects of drugs and toxins on livestock.
•	Animal Nutrition Laboratory – For analyzing and preparing balanced animal feed and supplements.
2. Artificial Insemination & Livestock Training Facility
a. Well-equipped AI Laboratories:
•	Training students in semen collection, processing, and artificial insemination techniques to improve cattle breeding programs.
•	Hands-on practice with AI equipment and protocols under the guidance of veterinary specialists.
b. Semen Storage Facility:
•	A state-of-the-art semen storage center to preserve high-quality semen for breeding programs.
•	This facility will also serve as a training center for cryopreservation techniques used in artificial insemination.
c. Demonstration & Livestock Handling Area:
•	A designated livestock demonstration unit with live animals for practical training in disease prevention, vaccination, and livestock care.
